# Documentation Synchronization Rules

Keep documentation aligned with real code.

## After Planning Changes

Update:

- requirements
- tasks
- SDD
- architecture notes
- open questions

## After Implementation Changes

Update documentation if:

- architecture changed
- APIs changed
- schemas changed
- setup changed
- dependencies changed
- environment variables changed
- background jobs changed
- security behavior changed
- deployment behavior changed

## SDD Accuracy

The SDD must distinguish:

```text
Implemented
Partial
Planned
Needs clarification
Deprecated
```

Do not describe planned features as implemented.

## Changelog

If useful, maintain:

```text
/ai-agent-workflow/changelog.md
```

Include:

- date
- task/phase
- summary
- changed files/modules
- tests
- known limitations

## Documentation Quality

Docs should be:

- accurate
- concise
- structured
- easy to follow
- free from fake implementation claims

## Comprehensive code reference

For engine packages, maintain `specs/code-reference/*.md` with every public file and symbol documented (**purpose**, **why**, **called by**). See `.cursor/rules/13-comprehensive-spec-documentation.mdc`.
